{"what":"What the hand-made derivative of src/ias/reg.js gains over a finite-difference matrix, as Henon (1974) used (Bulirsch-Stoer with regularisation inside a corrector, the matrix by finite increments of 1e-7). The option --matrix=exact|fd-forward|fd-central of tools/family-follow-ias.mjs builds the 12 x 12 matrix of every flagged piece and of every piece replaced by the cross-check from the derivative of reg.js (exact, the default), by forward differences with the increment 1e-7 * max(1, |x_c|) (fd-forward, Henon's increment) or by central differences with 1e-5 * max(1, |x_c|) (fd-central); the end state is that of the unperturbed flow in all three (it is the same to the last bit with and without the matrix). Part 1: the error of the three matrices on the 10 flagged pieces with the smallest pair distance of data/deep/extra/piece-check-mp.json. Part 2: the corrector of the driver with each variant on t35 - (31 recorded points) and t44 - (40 recorded points). Part 3: the verdict by the rule that was fixed before the runs.","reference_matrix":"central differences of the multiple precision flow of tools/refine-mp.py (the unregularised Gragg-Bulirsch-Stoer flow of tools/piece-mp.py) at 60 digits, tolerance 1e-42, step floor 1e-25, h = 1e-14 added to and subtracted from one start component (24 flows per piece, start states and tau of the 10 pieces as in data/deep/extra/piece-check-mp.json); the script that makes it is tools/fd-reference.py (the start state and tau of a piece from a file of tools/piece-ends.mjs). Check on the deepest piece (t35 - step 10 piece 17): the reference with h = 1e-14 and with h = 1e-12 agree to 7.7e-19 of the largest entry (the requirement was 1e-12); the unperturbed 60 digit flow of every piece agrees with its 50 digit end state of piece-check-mp.json to 3.3e-22 or better (field start_check).","matrix_error":"error = max over the 144 entries of |M - Mref| / max|Mref|","commands":["node tools/reproduce-trace.mjs t35m OUT.json --stop-after=31